      ":question/id": "0c401682-c55c-56ab-a54f-b7840f184808",
      ":question/problem": "$\\displaystyle\\int \\left(2-y^{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=$\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(2-y^{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y &= \\int \\left(2-y^{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &= 2\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}y-\\int y^{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &= 2\\frac{y^{0+1}}{(0+1)}-\\frac{y^{6+1}}{(6+1)}+C \\\\ &= 2y-\\frac{y^{7}}{7}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
